messages.content:
Crying "Ranjha, Ranjha," I have myself become Ranjha now.
Call me Dhido-Ranjha; let no one call me "Heer."
Ranjha is within me, and I within Ranjha — no other thought remains;
I am not: He alone is, consoling His own self.
Whatever dwells within us, that is our very essence;
the one I gave my love to, I have become just like him.
Cast off the white sheet, girl, and put on the faqir's coarse blanket;
the white sheet will show every stain — the blanket takes no stain.
Take me to Takht Hazara, Bulleh — among the Sials I find no refuge.
Crying "Ranjha, Ranjha," I have myself become Ranjha now.

What kind of repentance is this repentance? — do not repent like this, friend.
Repentance on the lips, not from the heart; from such repentance he gives up nothing;
what heedlessness has drawn its veil over you — why should the Forgiver forgive you?
Giving little and taking more, staking all on a gamble —
how would he ever attain true Islam, whose conduct is such as this?
You go where you should not, and take a stranger's blows;
you set the holy books on your head to swear — yet what trust can rest in you?
The tyrants have no fear of their tyranny; they die by their own doings;
they hold no fear of God — here and hereafter they are brought to disgrace.
What kind of repentance is this repentance? — do not repent like this, friend.
